      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a pretty imprecise way to describe a kinetic bottleneck. I'm not looking for \"magic\" or stories about \"friends playing tag\"—this is for a formal dissertation on organic chemistry.\n\nCan you please skip the analogies and provide the actual molecular mechanics? Specifically, I need the description of the enaminol intermediate's structure and the precise movement of the electrons during the keto-enol tautomerization that results in the Amadori product. What is the specific role of the nitrogen lone pair in the stabilization of the transition state during that intramolecular proton transfer?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
